  "summary": "The identified studies apply transformer-based architectures, specifically self-attention encoder models, to the domain of battery health, primarily focusing on estimating battery remaining life. These models were evaluated across several datasets including CellLife, ProtMap, GridWatch, and ToxiBench [V0077, V0080, V0079, V0078]. Reported performance metrics vary, with AUROC values reaching 0.87 on CellLife and accuracy reported at 0.66 on GridWatch [V0077, V0079]. One study reported an F1 score of 0.94 on ToxiBench [V0078]. Additionally, a related study on the same topic utilized decentralised training without pooled records [V0084].",
